            %h6 Definition
            %p
              An
              %strong involution
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism"} endomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              with itself is the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity morphism
            #eq:InvolutiveProperty.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi σ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi id
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\sigma \circ \sigma \;=\; id
                    \\,.
            %p
          Such an endomorphism is necessarily an
          = succeed "," do
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism"} automorphism
          = succeed "." do
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+morphism"} inverse
          %p
          #InvolutionsAreZModTwoActions.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (involutions are equivalently
                = succeed "-actions)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
              %br/
              Involutions are equivalently the value on the single non-trivial element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group+of+order+2"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+action"} group action
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
            %p
              In this guise, involutions appear throughout
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transformation+groups"} transformation groups
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+theory"} equivariant homotopy theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant cohomology
            %p
              In particular, involutions, are the defining ingredients of
              %em Real
              (with capital “R”!)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead-generalized+cohomology+theories"} Whitehead-generalized cohomology theories
              such as
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KR-theory"} KR-theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MR-theory"} MR-theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPR-theory"} BPR-theory
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ER-theory"} ER-theory
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (terminology in algebra)
              %br/
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
              equipped with an anti-involution is called a
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-algebra"} star-algebra
            %p
              On
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras"} algebras
              and other
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+structures"} mathematical structures
              where this makes sense, an
              %strong anti-involution
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-homomorphism"} anti-homomorphism
              satisfying
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:InvolutiveProperty"} (1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              (hence an anti-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism"} endomorphism
              and necessarily an anti-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism"}> automorphism
              ).
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (terminology in topology)
              %br/
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              equipped with an involutive
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
              is sometimes called a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+space"} real space
              (at least in the context of
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KR-theory"} KR-theory
            %p
              In view of Rem.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InvolutionsAreZModTwoActions"}
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+G-spaces"} topological G-spaces
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo =
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G =
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group+of+order+2"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-spheres"} n-spheres
              with involution is discussed
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "group+actions+on+spheres#Involutions"} here
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#commuting_involutions Commuting involutions
          %p
            Two involutions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f, g \colon X \to X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+diagram"} commute
            if and only if their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f g
            is also an involution, as shown by the following manipulations:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi f
                          %mi g
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo =
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi g
                          %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
