          %h3#fixed_point_free_involutions Fixed point free involutions
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorics"} combinatorics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point"} fixed point
            free ones: an arbitrary involution on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
            of cardinality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            may be specified by the choice of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            elements which are fixed together with a fixed point free involution on the remaining
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-k)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2n
            labelled elements is counted by the double factorial
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo !
                    %mo !
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi …
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mn 3
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo !
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mn 2
                          %mi n
                        %mi n
                        %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2n-1)!! = (2n-1)\cdot (2n-3)\cdot\dots\cdot 3\cdot 1 = \frac{(2n)!}{2^n n!}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            labelled elements are counted by OEIS sequence
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "https://oeis.org/A000085"} A000085
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Young+tableaux"} Young tableaux
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            cells.
          %h3#MonadOfInvolutions Monad of involutions
          %p
            An involution on a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the same thing as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 2
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z}
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            More generally, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,\otimes,1)
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+monoidal+category"} distributive
            finite
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 = 1 + 1
            is equipped with an involution
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi not
                  %mo :
                  %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  not : 2 \to 2
          %p
            defined as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copairing"} copairing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi not
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi inr
                  %mo ,
                  %mi inl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} not = [inr,inl]
            of the right and left injections. Moreover, 2 can be given the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi false
                  %mo :
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mi xor
                  %mo :
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} false : 1 \to 2 \qquad xor : 2 \otimes 2 \to 2
          %p
            defined by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi false
                  %mo =
                  %mi inl
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} false = inl
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi xor
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi id
                  %mo ,
                  %mi not
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} xor = [id,not]
            (here we make use of the isomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ≅
                  %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 \otimes 2 \cong 2 + 2
            to define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi xor
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} xor
            by copairing). The mapping
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi X
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi X
                  %mo +
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X \mapsto 2 \otimes X \cong X + X
          %p
            thus extends to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the free object equipped with an involution over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi η
                    %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_X : X \to 2\otimes X
            and the multiplication
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_X : 2\otimes 2\otimes X \to 2\otimes X
            of the monad are defined by tensoring the unit and the multiplication of the monoid with the identity on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 \otimes X
            is likewise defined by tensoring the involution on 2 with the identity on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            We then have that involutions in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            are precisely the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+over+a+monad"} algebras
            of the monad
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi false
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi xor
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2\otimes-,false\otimes-,xor\otimes-)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo :
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha : 2\otimes X \to X
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi id
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha = [id,f]
            (again using the isomorphism
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi X
                    %mo +
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2\otimes X \cong X+X
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo :
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha : 2\otimes X \to X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to X
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mi α
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi inr
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = \alpha \circ inr
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi inr
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi α
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi inr
                  %mo =
                  %mi α
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi inr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi inr
                  %mo =
                  %mi α
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi xor
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi id
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi inr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi inr
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \circ inr \circ \alpha \circ inr = \alpha \circ (2\otimes \alpha) \circ (2\otimes inr) \circ inr = \alpha \circ (xor\otimes id) \circ (2\otimes inr) \circ inr
          %p
            and since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi xor
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} xor
            is defined such that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi xor
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi id
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi inr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi inr
                    %mo =
                    %mi id
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (xor\otimes id) \circ (2\otimes inr) \circ inr = id
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi inr
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \circ inr
            is an involution.
